WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.840
While plenty of your favorite movies actually
get the critical acclaim and box office success

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:09.000
they deserve, there are some amazing films
that just don't seem to click with an audience.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.120
Still, just because a film wasn't a box office
success at first release doesn't mean that

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:14.340
it's not worth your time.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:18.340
Here are some genuinely great movies from
this decade that bombed at the box office.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:20.120
Free Fire

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:25.640
British director Ben Wheatley, who made the
modern horror masterpiece Kill List, quietly

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:27.720
dropped Free Fire in 2017.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:32.100
Hardly anybody saw it, but Free Fire has got
all the makings of a cult classic.

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:36.620
The film is a lean romp that takes place almost
entirely inside a single warehouse.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:40.800
Free Fire tells the story of an arms deal
gone wrong, leaving all the lowlifes involved

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.090
trapped with nothing but their wits and a
whole lot of guns to get them out.

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:48.180
It's filled with offbeat humor, one-liners,
and physical comedy that nicely breaks the

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.160
tension here and there.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:53.200
"Hey Vern, is everybody like you where you
come from?"

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.720
"Vern is a rare and mysterious jewel.”

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:58.760
Tomorrowland

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:04.760
A fun, exuberant, and inventive science fiction
tale, Tomorrowland was one of the better science-fiction

00:01:04.769 --> 00:01:06.500
films of the last 10 years.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:10.939
The film features George Clooney as a reclusive
genius inventor who meets a science-crazed

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:11.640
teenage girl.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:16.180
Their adventures center around Tomorrowland,
an alternate dimension of scientific wonder.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:20.440
Full of twists, turns, and some compelling
sci-fi concepts under director Brad Bird's

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:23.680
expert direction, Tomorrowland deserved to
be a huge hit.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:33.880
Scott Pilgrim vs. The World

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:38.350
There are movies that fail at the box office
that are only guilty of being released a few

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:42.560
years too early, and it was clear from the
first trailer that Scott Pilgrim vs. The World

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:43.460
was ahead of its time.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:47.340
Director Edgar Wright chose to ramp up the
comic book and video game influence on the

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.259
story all the way to 11.

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:53.680
Bad guys explode into piles of coins and sound
effects appear written out on the screen.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:57.920
It's a self-aware and self-referential film
winking at the audience constantly and packed

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:00.480
to the gills with nostalgia for classic video
games.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:04.950
If released in today's age of metatextual
pop culture, the film probably would have

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:05.940
been a massive success.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:07.340
"Hi.

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:08.480
Big fan."

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:11.540
"Why wouldn't you be?"

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:13.920
Popstar: Never Stop Never Stopping

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:19.350
A fake documentary spoofing concert-biopics
of modern pop sensations should be a onenote

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:23.160
journey with a few good jabs about Instagram
culture and autotune at best.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:27.660
Instead, Popstar: Never Stop Never Stopping
turned into one of the best mainstream comedies

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:29.040
of 2016.

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:34.210
Created by comedy music group The Lonely Island,
the film stars Andy Samberg as Conner, a Justin

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:35.820
Bieber-esque pop star on the rise.

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:39.800
It's got plenty of laughs, but what's more
surprising is how much heart is hidden beneath

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:41.280
its many celebrity cameos.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:45.790
Unfortunately, it underperformed at the box
office, but we think time is going to be kind

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:46.340
to this one.

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:52.740
"A nun dunks a basketball, living the impossible,
a man breaks his leg inside a hospital.

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:55.160
We just thought of that and it could change
the world."

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:56.740
Dredd

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:02.760
Lean, relentless, and running at a breakneck
pace, Dredd is a viscerally satisfying sci-fi

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:06.660
action film adapted from the long-running
british comic series Judge Dredd.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:11.170
The film sees future super-cop Judge Dredd
and his trainee, Judge Anderson, trapped in

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:14.520
a massive skyscraper with hundreds of armed
thugs out to kill them.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:18.640
Leading the gang of criminals is Ma-ma, a
notorious drug dealer played with ruthless

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:20.660
relish by Game of Thrones’ Lena Heady.

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:24.620
The film is a violent, brutal romp, taking
Dredd and Anderson up through the building's

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:27.800
many floors in increasingly inventive action
sequences.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:31.700
"This block operates under the same rules
as the rest of the city.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.040
Ma-Ma is not the law.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:37.360
I am the law."

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:39.080
Premium Rush

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:44.480
An action-crime story set in the world of
fixed-gear bike messengers shouldn't work,

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:46.840
and yet somehow, Premium Rush is fantastic.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:50.640
Premium Rush is anchored by the excellent
Michael Shannon, who really shines in his

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:51.820
role as a crooked cop.

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:56.340
As he relentlessly pursues Joseph Gordon-Levitt's
bike messenger character throughout New York

00:03:56.340 --> 00:04:00.720
City, the film showcases some killer chase
sequences and well-edited action scenes.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:05.120
The film's nonlinear narrative seals the deal,
making Premium Rush a whole lot of fun and

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:06.480
very much worth your time.

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:07.920
Warrior

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:13.040
The story of two brothers separated as teenagers
who find themselves forced to fight one another

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:17.800
in a mixed martial arts tournament sounds
cliche at first glance, but Warrior is surprisingly

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:18.300
powerful.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:22.440
The brothers, played by Joel Edgerton and
Tom Hardy have gone down different paths since

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:26.690
their separation but are perpetually tied
together by their alcoholic screw-up father.

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:31.450
Warrior is very much Rocky for the UFC generation,
and the movie packs the same emotional punch

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:33.500
of Sylvester Stallone's seminal classic.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:36.260
This is one you shouldn't miss, but make sure
you bring tissues.

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:37.140
You'll need them.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:40.580
"You're not the only one who's suffered Tommy.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:43.660
I didn't even know she was sick."

